BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Queers to the Front!
UID:event_315885473@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041436Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T150000
SUMMARY:Let’s Craft!
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nGreetings everyone! Let’s get together
  and craft while snacking on pie! You can bring whatever craft you’re in
 to\, though please don’t bring anything too big/messy (e.g. no mural pai
 nting) since we want everyone to have space to work and need to leave the 
 place spotless!\n\nThe Baked Pie Company has an ever rotating selection of
  award-winning pies (as well as quiche and salad)\; they even have pie fli
 ghts! They also feature sugar free\, gluten free\, keto and vegan pies for
  those with dietary needs. So let's grab a slice of pie and build some com
 munity!\n\nDon't worry if you can't make this one\, though! It’s a month
 ly event\; you'll have plenty of chances to get your pie on :)\n\nYou can 
 check out the menu here:\nhttps://www.bakedpiecompany.com/list-of-pies
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/315885473/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260729T052417Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T052417Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Queers to the Front!
UID:event_316333514@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041436Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260922T203000
SUMMARY:Sapphic Book Club!  - July
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nOur book club read for September is *Bur
 y Our Bones in the Midnight Soil* by V.E. Schwab.\n\n*This is a story abou
 t hunger.*\n\n**1532\\. Santo Domingo de la Calzada\\.**\nA young girl gro
 ws up wild and wily—her beauty is only outmatched by her dreams of escap
 e. But María knows she can only ever be a prize\, or a pawn\, in the game
 s played by men. When an alluring stranger offers an alternate path\, Mar
 ía makes a desperate choice. She vows to have no regrets.\n\n*This is a s
 tory about love.*\n**1827\\. London\\.**\nA young woman lives an idyllic b
 ut cloistered life on her family’s estate\, until a moment of forbidden 
 intimacy sees her shipped off to London. Charlotte’s tender heart and se
 emingly impossible wishes are swept away by an invitation from a beautiful
  widow—but the price of freedom is higher than she could have imagined.\
 n\n*This is a story about rage.*\n**2019\\. Boston\\.**\nCollege was suppo
 sed to be her chance to be someone new. That’s why Alice moved halfway a
 cross the world\, leaving her old life behind. But after an out-of-charact
 er one-night stand leaves her questioning her past\, her present\, and her
  future\, Alice throws herself into the hunt for answers . . . and revenge
 .\n\n***This is a story about life—***\n***how it ends\, and how it star
 ts.***\n\n++\n\n[Read full synopsis here at The StoryGraph](https://app.th
 estorygraph.com/books/bcef7254-c9a4-48a8-8c0c-d6bc7f5cecd6)\n\n***\\*\\*\\
 ****\n\nWe'll meet at **White Duck Taco** in South Asheville \\(off Long S
 hoals Rd\\) \\|\\| Come early if you want some yummy food and drinks\\!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/316333514/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260830T020812Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260830T020812Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Queers to the Front!
UID:event_315151068@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041436Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T210000
SUMMARY:Josie Beers Gets Weirds
DESCRIPTION:Queers to the Front!\nModelface Comedy Club brings the best co
 medians from all over the country to Asheville\, NC. This week we are exci
 ted to have local legend Josie Beers!\n\nJoise Beers Gets Weirds\nInside J
 osie Beers are two dragons. One is a 83 year old Korean war vet\, and the 
 other\, a powerful thirty-something transwoman. After escaping the shutdow
 n mines of central Pennsylvania and taming her inner dragons\, she calls W
 NC home.\n\nfeaturing Derek Boskovich\n\nages 18+\nDoors at 6:30pm\, show 
 at 7pm\nTickets $15
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/queers-to-the-front/events/315151068/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260607T205337Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260607T205337Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
